' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Herencia de mixins
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PrimaryKeyMixin <|-- ChannelAccount
ActiveMixin     <|-- ChannelAccount
SoftDeleteMixin <|-- ChannelAccount
TimestampMixin  <|-- ChannelAccount

PrimaryKeyMixin <|-- Conversation
ActiveMixin     <|-- Conversation
SoftDeleteMixin <|-- Conversation
TimestampMixin  <|-- Conversation

PrimaryKeyMixin <|-- Message
PrimaryKeyMixin <|-- MessageAttachment
PrimaryKeyMixin <|-- ConversationAssignmentLog

note bottom of TimestampMixin
  **Mixins por entidad (modelo final)**
  • Los 4 mixins (con ""SoftDeleteMixin""):
    ""ChannelAccount"", ""Conversation""
    (datos de negocio vivos).
  • PK·A·T (SIN ""SoftDeleteMixin""):
    ""Message"", ""MessageAttachment"",
    ""ConversationAssignmentLog""
    (audit trail inmutable — un mensaje
    recibido/enviado es un hecho).
  (Sólo se dibujan las herencias completas;
  los logs/mensajes muestran solo ""PrimaryKeyMixin"".)
end note

' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Repos extienden el genérico BaseRepository<ModelT>
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
BaseRepository <|-- ChannelAccountRepository            : "<ChannelAccount>"
BaseRepository <|-- ConversationRepository              : "<Conversation>"
BaseRepository <|-- MessageRepository                   : "<Message>"
BaseRepository <|-- MessageAttachmentRepository         : "<MessageAttachment>"
BaseRepository <|-- ConversationAssignmentLogRepository : "<ConversationAssignmentLog>"

' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Relaciones de dominio (FK + relationship reales)
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ChannelAccount "1" -- "0..*" Conversation : "abre"
Conversation   "1" -- "0..*" Message
Message        "1" -- "0..*" MessageAttachment
Conversation   "1" -- "0..*" ConversationAssignmentLog : "handoff"

' FKs reales hacia user (admin.user ya existe) y person (crm existe)
Conversation              "*" -- "0..1" Person : "person_id (FK)"
Conversation              "*" -- "0..1" User   : "advisor (assignee, FK)"
Message                   "*" -- "0..1" User   : "sender (si advisor, FK)"
ConversationAssignmentLog "*" -- "0..1" User   : "from/to/by (FK)"

' Forward FKs (ADR-009): SOLO columna varchar(36), SIN FK/relationship.
' El módulo dueño (bots/marketing) agrega la constraint luego → línea punteada.
ChannelAccount ..> BotConfiguration : "bot_configuration_id (default)\n<<forward FK, ADR-009>>"
ChannelAccount ..> Campaign         : "default_campaign_id (atribución)\n<<forward FK, ADR-009>>"
Conversation   ..> BotConfiguration : "bot_configuration_id (efectivo)\n<<forward FK, ADR-009>>"
Message        ..> BotConfiguration : "bot_configuration_id\n<<forward FK, ADR-009>>"

' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Repos manejan su modelo
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ChannelAccountRepository            ..> ChannelAccount
ConversationRepository              ..> Conversation
MessageRepository                   ..> Message
MessageAttachmentRepository         ..> MessageAttachment
ConversationAssignmentLogRepository ..> ConversationAssignmentLog

' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Webhook router delega a processors por canal
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
wh_router ..> wpw : delega (whatsapp)
wh_router ..> wpt : delega (telegram, futuro)
wh_router ..> ca_svc : carga ChannelAccount + get_credentials

' Processors usan services internos
wpw ..> conv_svc : find_or_create_open
wpw ..> msg_svc  : persist_inbound / apply_status
wpt ..> conv_svc
wpt ..> msg_svc

' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Services usan repos
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ca_svc   ..> ChannelAccountRepository
conv_svc ..> ConversationRepository
conv_svc ..> ConversationAssignmentLogRepository
msg_svc  ..> MessageRepository
msg_svc  ..> MessageAttachmentRepository

' Secret resolver consumido por channel_account.get_credentials (+ webhook firma + outbound)
ca_svc      ..> secrets_mod : resolve(secret_name)

' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Enganche aditivo con crm (3 helpers consumidos + 2 cambios aditivos)
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
conv_svc ..> crm_person_svc  : find_by_identifier_or_create\n(resolver Person en inbound)
conv_svc ..> crm_la_repo     : advisor_map\n(auto-asignar al dueño del lead)
conv_svc ..> crm_act_svc     : log(..., related_conversation_id)\n(CONVERSATION_TAKEN / RELEASED)
conv_svc ..> crm_person_repo : person_option_map\n(denorm ConversationListItem.person)

' FK aditiva (conversations es el dueño): lead_activity.related_conversation_id → conversation.id
LeadActivity ..> Conversation : "related_conversation_id\n<<FK aditiva F2 (Postgres-only), ADR-009>>"

' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Notas
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
note right of ChannelAccount
  **Multi-cuenta por canal**
  Mismo ""channel_type"" puede tener varias filas
  con distinto ""external_identifier"".
  ""channel_type"" REUSA el enum ""crm.ChannelType""
  (single source of truth — NO se duplica).
  Credencial en GCP Secret Manager, referenciada
  por ""secret_name"" (el valor NUNCA viaja al schema;
  el ""Detail"" expone ""credentials_configured: bool"").
end note

note right of Conversation
  **Una activa por (person, channel)**
  UNIQUE PARTIAL via ""status='open' AND deleted_at IS NULL"".
  Las cerradas viven como historial (reabrir tras cerrar).
  Auto-asignada al dueño del lead al nacer
  (fallback ""unassigned""); el asesor toma/libera/cierra.
end note

note bottom of secrets_mod
  **ADR-010 — secretos por-cuenta en runtime**
  El template inyecta secretos fijos por env (deploy-time,
  ""--set-secrets"" → ""Settings""). Para credenciales por
  ""ChannelAccount"" se introduce el SDK
  ""google-cloud-secret-manager"" + cache TTL + fallback env
  (local/test). Patrón reusable (bots lo consumirá).
  Cliente lazy → no rompe el boot sin GCP (smoke/sqlite).
end note

note bottom of msg_svc
  **Outbound real (Meta Graph API)**
  ""send_outbound"" persiste el ""Message"", resuelve
  ""access_token"" + ""phone_number_id"" vía
  ""ca.get_credentials"" → ""POST /{phone_number_id}/messages"".
  Falla → ""failed_at""/""failure_reason"", **200** con el
  message fallido (UI reintenta), NO 502. Reintento =
  ""Message"" nuevo (el fallido queda inmutable).
  **NO** emite ""MESSAGE_SENT"" por-mensaje (decisión §1).
end note

note bottom of conv_svc
  **Emisión a crm (timeline lead-céntrico)**
  Solo ""CONVERSATION_TAKEN"" (al tomar) y
  ""CONVERSATION_RELEASED"" (al liberar) vía
  ""crm.lead_activity.log(..., related_conversation_id)"".
  NO ""MESSAGE_SENT"". Estos tipos NO están en
  ""ADVISOR_ACTIVITY_TYPES"" → el composer de crm
  no puede editarlos/borrarlos (audit inmutable).
end note

note bottom of wh_router
  **Sin JWT — validación por firma del provider**
  WhatsApp: HMAC SHA256 del body RAW con ""app_secret""
  resuelto de Secret Manager (mismatch → 403).
  Procesamiento **síncrono** antes del 200 (MVP sin bot).
  Vive top-level (""app/routers/""), no en ""modules/"".
end note

note bottom of crm_act_svc
  **2 cambios aditivos a crm (backward-compatible)**
  #1 ""find_by_identifier_or_create"": advisory lock
     transaccional Postgres keyed por (channel_type,
     identifier) → serializa el get-then-insert ante
     webhooks concurrentes del mismo número nuevo.
  #2 ""lead_activity.log"": nuevo param opcional
     ""related_conversation_id"" (la columna ya existe).
  + FK aditiva ""lead_activity.related_conversation_id
     → conversation.id"" en la migración 0016 (Postgres-only).
  Sin ""relationship"" ORM cross-módulo (modelo crm intacto).
end note

@enduml
